nterleaving matches even when the `.so` is loaded by a C host.\n- Bugs preserved: `DISPATCH_REP` has no `case 7`, so `use_generated(7)` returns just `INIT` (0/0/1) — reproduced exactly; signed overflow reproduced with wrapping arithmetic.\n\n## Verification I ran myself\n- **Differential test: 24 feature combos (3 OP × 8 REPEAT) × 17 input cases** (normal, negative, overflowing `int`, `LONG_MAX`/`LONG_MIN` strings, `\"  12abc\"`, `\"x y\"`, `\"0x10\"`, missing args) — stdout, stderr, and exit codes byte-identical to gcc-built binaries: `DONE fail=0`.\n- **Shared-library ABI test**: a C program `dlopen`s both the gcc `.so` and the Rust `cdylib` and calls every exported symbol + globals — identical output for `add/5`, `sub/3`, `mul/6`, `add/0`, `mul/7`.\n- **Compile matrix**: 42 feature sets (each single feature, all OP×REPEAT pairs, overlapping/contradictory sets, `--all-features`, empty set) plus a `--release` build — all succeed with zero warnings."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":708,"cache_read_input_tokens":65730,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":708,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"03d57edd-0219-4077-bbd2-bff0dfc5126f","uuid":"c7904bf7-33b8-4b07-b53d-b6a4c4e091ee","timestamp":"2026-08-21T08:36:36.469Z"}
